```rust
/// The identity string recorded for an MCP server that failed to connect.
///
/// One definition, two call sites: the `Err` arm of the `[mcp_servers.*]`
/// connect loop (the writer) and `/mcp list` (the reader that marks the row).
/// Two copies of this format string would agree the day they are written and
/// diverge the first time one side is reworded — and the failure mode is
/// silent: the row simply stops being marked (#745/#767/#842 shape).
pub(crate) fn mcp_failed_server_id(name: &str, command: &str) -> String {
    format!("{name} ({command})")
}
```

And the CLI loop's id is just the raw command string, which is `mcp_cmd` — no helper needed.

