Committed as 324637f7. Here's what landed and what I verified.

## What I built

/mcp list now marks each server that failed to connect, so 2 of 3 failed no longer renders like 3 of 3 failed. The fact was already recorded by record_failed_server (agent_builder.rs, the single write site) — Day 181 gave the model a reader (external_tool_failure_note) and left the user with one dim startup line. This adds the second audience and moves neither store: no reconnection, no change to connections_lost_note, nothing on the model-facing path.

It marks only what it can prove. mcp_connected is a count, not a set, so no row claims success; and no tool name is ever invented, because a failed connect means yoyo never learned what that server exposes. openapi_failed is deliberately absent — /mcp list is the MCP surface.

Two ids, one shape each, shared with the writer rather than copied. The --mcp row records the raw command; a [mcp_servers.*] row records name (command). Matching is exact, so mcp_failed_server_id now builds that string for both the writer and the reader — a copied format string would agree today and diverge silently, marking no row and nothing else noticing. capped_failure_id + EXTERNAL_FAILURE_ID_MAX_BYTES likewise got one definition serving both audiences (char-boundary cut, #250, with the in-band byte count verified against what was actually dropped).

## One deviation from the task, and it's the better direction

STEP 0 told me to register commands_config.rs at 2029. I did that first — then the ~370 lines made the drift fatal, and the gate's own remedy is "paste the number or move the new code to a smaller module." I took the split: the new module src/commands_config_mcp.rs is a clean seam (those functions read nothing but their arguments, so no private helper had to be widened). That put commands_config.rs at 1999 — under the cap, so branch 3 fired and its register entry was deleted, not updated. Registering would have converted a paid debt into a permanent ceiling. handle_mcp's signature is unchanged.

## Verification

cargo build, cargo test (5672 passed), cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo fmt -- --check — all green. src_modules_respect_the_size_gate passes.

Positive control run as one atomic mutate→run→restore: neutering mcp_failure_marker to always return None reddened exactly the four failure-path tests by name while the no-failure byte-identity near-miss stayed green; restored, re-ran green. Marker removed from the tree.

Six tests: full-block assert_eq! for no failures, one failure, two failures, glyph-freedom in plain mode, an anti-vacuous companion on the fixture id, and the char-boundary cap.

One thing I did not over-claim: the old inline code put {RESET} before its trailing newlines, so the newline now falls inside the dim span. Visible characters and end-of-call colour state are identical (same shape /config show uses), but it is not stream-level byte-identity — so the assertions pin the colour-code-free block and say so. That is written into both the doc comment and ARCHITECTURE.md.

